# Tata Steel AI Hackathon — ML Method Organization

**Hackathon**: [Tata Steel AI Hackathon](https://www.hackerearth.com/community/challenges/competitive/tata-steel-ai-hackathon/)
**Problem statement**: [Machine Learning challenge](https://www.hackerearth.com/challenges/competitive/tata-steel-ai-hackathon/machine-learning/fd-a5a6dcb2/)

Tabular ML project (CoilID, features X1–X49, binary target Y). Shared data lives in `dataset/`.

## Folder structure

Each distinct method or algorithm gets its own folder under `models/`:

```
models/
  xgboost-baseline/
    README.md
    xgboost-baseline.ipynb   # Colab entry point
    train.py                 # local training (required)
    predict.py               # local inference (required)
    submission/              # HackerEarth upload bundle (required)
      approach.txt           # approach, feature engineering, tools (plain text)
      submission.csv         # prediction file (CoilID,Y) — copied from latest run
      source/                # relevant source copies (generated by pack script)
      xgboost-baseline-hackerearth.zip
    outputs/
      latest_run.txt
      latest/
      runs/<timestamp>/
        metrics.json
        predictions/submission.csv
        plots/
        artifacts/
```

**Rules:**
- One folder = one approach. Do not mix unrelated methods.
- Kebab-case folder names (e.g. `lightgbm-cv`, `neural-net-mlp`).
- Shared utilities in `utils/` — not inside method folders.
- Every method folder: `README.md`, `{name}.ipynb`, `train.py`, `predict.py`, `submission/`.

## Dual execution: Colab + local

Support **both** environments with the same artifact layout:

| Environment | Entry point | Default paths |
|-------------|-------------|---------------|
| **Local** | `python models/{name}/train.py` | Creates `outputs/runs/<timestamp>/` |
| **Colab** | `models/{name}/{name}.ipynb` | Mount Drive; set `REPO_ROOT`; save under same `outputs/runs/` |

Notebooks and scripts must use `utils/run_artifacts.py` so results land in the repo whether you train locally or on Colab.

### Local CLI convention

```bash
python models/{name}/train.py --data-dir dataset
python models/{name}/predict.py --data-dir dataset
python .cursor/skills/tata-steel-submission/scripts/pack_submission.py models/{name}
```

`predict.py` defaults to the run id in `outputs/latest_run.txt`. `pack_submission.py` validates, copies `submission.csv` into `submission/`, and builds `{name}-hackerearth.zip`.

## HackerEarth submission folder (`submission/`)

Each method must have `submission/` for [Round 1 uploads](https://www.hackerearth.com/challenges/competitive/tata-steel-ai-hackathon/machine-learning/fd-a5a6dcb2/):

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `submission.csv` | Prediction file — header `CoilID,Y`, one row per test ID, values 0/1 |
| `approach.txt` | Plain-text write-up: approach, feature engineering, tools/libraries, reproduction steps |
| `{name}-hackerearth.zip` (or `.tar.gz`) | Archive containing `approach.txt` + `source/` (notebook, train.py, predict.py, README, utils) |

Workflow after train + predict:

1. Write or update `submission/approach.txt` (intricate technical detail — not a one-liner).
2. Run `pack_submission.py models/{name}` — copies latest predictions, bundles source, validates CSV.
3. Upload to HackerEarth: **prediction CSV** + **source zip/tar** as separate deliverables.

Commit `submission/approach.txt`, `submission/submission.csv`, and the archive. Regenerate the zip after every meaningful model change before upload.

## Saved outputs (required after every train run)

Persist under `outputs/runs/<timestamp>/` — never leave metrics/plots only in notebook display or `/tmp`:

### `artifacts/` (inside each run)

- Serialized model (e.g. `xgb_model.json`)
- Preprocessing objects (`imputer.joblib`)
- `meta.joblib` — threshold, hyperparameters, seeds, feature list

### Run root + `plots/` + `predictions/`

- `metrics.json` — OOF PR-AUC, OOF accuracy @ threshold, per-fold scores, majority baseline
- `run_config.json` — data path, hyperparameters
- `oof_predictions.csv` — CoilID, y_true, oof_proba, oof_pred
- `plots/` — PNG (150 dpi+): PR curve, threshold sweep, confusion matrix, feature importance, fold scores
- `predictions/submission.csv` — HackerEarth format (`CoilID,Y`)

After each run, call `copy_to_latest_summary(method_dir, run_dir)` to populate `outputs/latest/`.

Update `README.md` **Results** from `outputs/latest/metrics.json` after each meaningful run.

### Git

**Commit:** source code, `README.md`, `approach.txt`, `dataset/`, skills, notebooks.

**Do not commit** (see root `.gitignore`; regenerate locally):

- `models/*/outputs/` — train runs, models, plots, metrics
- `models/*/submission/source/`, `submission.csv`, `*-hackerearth.zip`, `pack_meta.json`

After clone: `train.py` → `predict.py` → `pack.py`.

## Google Colab notebooks (`.ipynb`)

1. **Setup** — `%pip install ...`; detect Colab vs local
2. **Paths** — `REPO_ROOT`, `DATA_DIR`, `RUN_DIR = create_run_dir(METHOD_DIR)`
3. **GPU check** — when using neural nets / GPU libraries
4. **Reproducibility** — seeds + version logging
5. **Train → validate → predict** — same pipeline as `train.py`; save all outputs to `RUN_DIR`
6. **Export** — `predictions/submission.csv`; optional Colab download cell

Prefer shared logic in `train.py` / `predict.py` and `utils/`; notebooks call the same helpers.

## Required README.md per method

1. **Method** — algorithm, libraries, hyperparameters
2. **Why this approach** — hypothesis, strengths, trade-offs
3. **Technical details** — preprocessing, CV, imbalance, threshold, leakage guards, output layout
4. **Results** — from latest `outputs/latest/metrics.json`; leaderboard if submitted
5. **How to run** — Colab steps **and** local `train.py` / `predict.py` commands

Write with intricate technical depth. Avoid vague one-liners.

## When adding or modifying code

- New algorithm or materially different pipeline → new folder under `models/`.
- Refactoring within same method → update `README.md` and re-save outputs.
- Scaffold: `README.md`, `{name}.ipynb`, `train.py`, `predict.py`, `pack.py`, `submission/approach.txt`.
